# Build context excludes. The API image builds from the REPO ROOT (see
# apps/api/Dockerfile), so everything here is relative to the root.
#
# The critical entry is node_modules. The deps stage runs `pnpm install` to
# populate /repo/node_modules for linux, and the build stage then does
# `COPY . .` — without this file that copy drops the HOST's node_modules on top,
# replacing linux binaries with darwin ones and breaking argon2, esbuild and
# @swc/core at build time. It also drags ~1GB through the context on every
# build.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Secrets. Nothing in the image needs these, and the build stage would otherwise
# bake them into a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output — regenerated inside the image, and stale host copies would mask
# a genuinely broken build.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Not needed to build or run the API.
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.specify
.vercel
**/.vercel
apps/web
tools
specs
docker
docker-compose.yml
*.md
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Belt and braces. `*.md` above is root-only under Docker's matcher, so the
# rubric the seed reads is already safe — but say so explicitly, because the
# seed fails in a confusing way if this file ever goes missing from the context.
!apps/api/prisma/seed/rubric-v1.md
